WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.540
"Reversible Causes
of Premature Hair Graying"

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.280
The graying of hair,

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.920
the age-related "exhaustion
of the pigmentary potential"

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.200
is thought to be mainly genetic,

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.640
with a family history
of premature graying

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.680
present in up to 90 percent
of cases.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.360
But if the rate of graying
is caused by oxidative damage,

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.720
as I described
in the last video,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.080
what role might be played
by antioxidants

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.280
and systemic oxidative stress

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.560
outside of the hair follicle?

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.600
Those with premature graying
do seem to have

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.240
higher circulating markers
of oxidative damage

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.120
and lower antioxidant levels
in blood.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.800
The higher prevalence of
premature graying among smokers

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.960
also supports this possibility
that exogenous free radicals

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.040
may speed up the accumulation
of oxidative insults

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.520
in the aging hair follicle.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.200
Obese individuals
also tend to gray early,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.320
consistent with
the oxidative stress concept,

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.400
though drinkers do not.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.080
Alcohol consumption clearly
causes oxidative stress

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:11.440
yet is not
significantly associated

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.760
with premature graying.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.320
Those trying to maximize
their intake of antioxidants

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.000
by eating plant-based

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.480
must deal with
the Achilles heel-

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.960
the risk of
vitamin B12 deficiency

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.320
for those not actively
supplementing their diets

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.720
with B12,

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.160
whether from supplements
or fortified foods.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:33.520
B12 deficiency is one
of the rare reversible causes

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.760
of hair graying through
some unknown mechanism.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:41.360
Thankfully, hair can repigment
after B12 repletion.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:45.280
Another reversible cause
is hypothyroidism,

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.440
which can be reversed with
thyroid hormone replacement.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.960
Rather than oxidative stress,
what about regular stress?

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:57.720
Does fight-or-flight
turn hair white?

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.160
Marie Antoinette syndrome

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.720
refers to the rapid graying of
hair due to stress or trauma,

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.960
based on the (likely apocryphal)
story of her hair going

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:11.720
completely white
on the eve of her beheading.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.520
Sporadic validated reports
of sudden graying

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.680
have been attributed
to the sudden diffuse loss

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.240
of pigmented hairs,

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.360
leaving the gray hairs behind,

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.840
offering the illusion
of transmogrification.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.840
In mice, acute stressors
can lead to hair graying

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.640
via rapid depletion
of melanocyte stem cells,

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.000
perhaps because
psychological stress

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.280
may lead to oxidative stress

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.920
(based on cross-sectional
studies that link higher

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:45.400
perceived stress to higher
levels of oxidative DNA damage).

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.280
Why might we even have evolved

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.080
to turn gray
in response to stress?

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:54.080
Drawing on an analogy
from the authority afforded

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:56.480
silverback mountain gorillas,

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.600
stress-induced graying
may confer

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:01.840
a "school of hard knocks"
evolutionary advantage

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.400
for leadership.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.040
For real-world consequences,

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.600
check out the results
of this study:

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.640
hospitalized patients

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:12.960
treated by gray-haired
attending physicians

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.960
were found to be
significantly more likely

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.880
to make it
out of the hospital alive

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:21.280
than those attended
by dark or blond-haired docs.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:25.440
As a mark of age, gray hair may
also be a mark of experience.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.000
But might having
gray hair yourself

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.200
increase your own chances
of ending up in the hospital?

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.200
Might premature
or extensive graying

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.400
be a sign of accelerated aging

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.760
and subsequent risk
of age-related diseases?

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.600
The data is mixed.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.040
Some studies suggest
the degree of graying

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.720
is an independent risk factor
for coronary artery disease,

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.960
for example based on higher
coronary calcium scores

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.200
in grayer individuals.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.120
However,
by far the largest study,

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:00.400
which followed 13,000
men and women for 16 years,

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.360
found no correlation
between graying

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:04.840
(or hair loss or wrinkles)

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.800
and overall mortality.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:10.080
The only exception appeared
to be a small fraction of men

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.560
without any gray hair

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:14.440
(just 6 percent
of those in their 50s,

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.360
2 percent of those in their 60s,

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.000
and 1 percent
of those in their 70s),

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:29.600
who did seem to have a
significantly lower mortality.

